According to Article 2(2), the following types of processing activities fall outside the material scope of this Regulation:

(a) Processing of personal data in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law;
(b) Processing by the Member States when carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU;
(c) Processing by a natural person in the course of a purely personal or household activity;
(d) Processing by competent authorities for the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offenses.

This information is sourced from CELEX_02016R0679-20160504_EN_TXT.pdf, p.2.
